WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:02.960
We all sleep.

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:07.200
And by “we all” I mean all animals

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.360
from bugs to bird to people.

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:13.330
And sleep looks the same on us, from the outside.

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:17.320
We lie down, close our eyes, stay still

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:19.150
But on the inside

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:21.570
- what our brains are doing during sleep -

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:25.160
was thought to be unique to birds and mammals.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.320
During sleep for these animals, the brain exhibits

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.540
two different patterns of activity -

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.660
slow-wave sleep and rapid-eye movement or REM sleep.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:37.180
But now, it looks like reptiles

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:40.320
have a similar pattern of activity in their sleep:

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.680
REM sleep alternating with a slow-wave type sleep

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.380
throughout the resting period.

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:48.100
Researchers were able to measure this type of sleep

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.740
in lizards for the first time using implanted electrodes,

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:55.580
infrared cameras and elaborate analysis.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.820
One unique aspect of lizard sleep -

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:03.160
the lizard’s sleep cycle is only about 60-90 seconds long

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:05.760
In humans, our complex sleep cycles

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:08.640
last 60-90 minutes each!

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:10.280
Does this mean that lizards

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.680
have short, frequent dreams?

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:15.000
It’s still too early to tell if lizards

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.439
or even birds dream during their sleep

00:01:17.439 --> 00:01:20.419
But what we do know is that our sleep patterns

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:22.720
are a lot older than once thought—

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:24.939
at least 300 million years old.

00:01:24.939 --> 00:01:27.399
Because lizards may be more similar to

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.420
our shared common ancestor,

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:32.760
studying sleep in the reptile brain may be the best way

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:36.360
to learn more about how sleep works for everyone.

